<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Contract</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>offer &lt;player&gt;       ask what it would cost
contract &lt;player&gt;    pay, and have the player killed
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>contract Mayor
</pre>
<p>Mercenaries will kill other players for money: the Assassin who walks the
streets of Midgaard is one (he starts out on Colosseum Road). Stand before
one and name your victim. If you can pay, the money is taken at once, the
mercenary says "Consider them dead", sneaks and hides its way to the victim
wherever they are, and attacks. It keeps after the victim until they are
dead, takes what is in the corpse, and then vanishes in a blue cloud and
returns to where you hired it. If it loses the victim's trail, it gives up
and returns the same way.
</p><p>A contract costs 20 platinum pieces, and a little more the higher the
victim's level. If you can't pay, the mercenary tells you the price;
offer tells you the same price without paying.
</p><p>A mercenary takes no contract on:
</p>
<ul><li>a player of level 20 or below: "Killing of newbies is not permitted!"</li>
<li>an immortal, or a monster: fight your own battles</li>
<li>yourself, or a player who is dead (a spirit), or one it can't find</li>
<li>anyone while it is still out on another job</li></ul>
<p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Assassins</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Player Killing</a>
</pre>




</div>